+++ b/evidence/04-satisfying-witnesses.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+Entry claim witnesses and ground substitutions
+================================================
+
+trial-correct precondition:
+  C = 4, D = 2, B = true, N = 5, K = .K.
+  C >= 2 and D >= 2 is true.
+  noFactor(4, 2) = false because 2 * 2 <= 4 and 4 % 2 = 0.
+  The claimed RHS is scan(5, 5) ~> prependIf(4, false), which evaluates to nil.
+
+scan-correct precondition:
+  C = 2, N = 5, K = .K.
+  C >= 2 is true.
+  primesFrom(2, 5) = cons(2, cons(3, nil)).
+
+count-up-to-correct entry precondition:
+  N = 5.
+  N >= 0 is true, the initial result cell is .K, and the parsed program is the
+  constructor tree in solution.mpy.
+  primesBelow(5) = primesFrom(2, 5) = cons(2, cons(3, nil)).
+  Both trusted canonical.py and candidate solution.py return the Python list
+  [2, 3]; fresh krun also returns cons(2, cons(3, nil)).
+
+Additional entry boundary witness:
+  N = 0 satisfies N >= 0.
+  primesBelow(0) = nil, both Python implementations return [], and fresh krun
+  returns nil.
+
+Machine evidence:
+  03-kprove-trial.log
+  03-kprove-scan.log
+  03-kprove-entry.log
+  03-krun-n0.log
+  03-krun-n20.log
+  03-concrete-compare.log
